face-image: img/redfront.jpg

= May Day, 1929

Tensions run high in Berlin. The We are planning a demonstration to commemorate the 10th anniversary of the Spartacist Uprising. No one has forgotten that it was the SPD who ordered the uprising's suppression and caused the deaths of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht.

Many non-communists are afraid of the possibility of another violent uprising, and the right wing of the Prussian coalition are asking the Prussian Interior Ministry to ban our demonstrations.

- @ban: The SPD bans our demonstrations.
- @allow_police: Our demonstrations are allowed to proceed, but only with a heavy police presence.
- @allow: Our demonstrations proceed, without a police presence.
- @join: Let the SPD join?

@ban
on-arrival: blutmai = 1; spd_relation -= 25; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; workers_kpd += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3; communist_coalition -= 3; strife += 1
face-image: img/blutmai.jpg

Our demonstration has been banned, and  police are sent to enforce the ban. There was a confrontation between the police and our demonstrators, and violence erupted. Reports say that the Berlin police killed dozens of demonstrators and innocent bystanders. The SPD have really proven themselves as social fascist and we won't forget this bloody May incident.

This may crush any hope of reconciliation or cooperation between our party. How are they going to explain themselves

- @communist_fault: Despite it being THEM who slaughter innocents, we are to blame.
- @no_fault: The incident is an unforunate tradegy, nobody is to blame and that includes us.


@communist_fault
choose-if: spd_relation <=15
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD finds this course of action excessive.
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 10; rfb_strength -= 80; rfb_banned = 1

Claiming that we had acted illegally, The Prussian coalition has banned the RFB. This will make any rallies in Prussia more difficult without the RFB to defend us. [? if united_front_maintained == 0: We've previously downplayed the Comintern's social fascist narrative in our press in hopes of cooperation, but this event turns much of the party firmly against the SPD. ?]

@no_fault

To our suprise, we aren't blamed for this. The RFB has remained untouched but we are still suspicous of the social fascists nonetheless. 


@allow_police
choose-if: spd_relation <=25 and spd_relation >15
unavailable-subtitle: Their centrist coalition partners dissuade them from this.
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5; workers_kpd += 5; unemployed_kpd += 5

The SPD has choosen to allow the demonstration, perhaps due to our improved relations. Onlookers admire the strength of our workers with some even joining the party.


@allow
choose-if: spd_relation <=35 and spd-relations >25
unavailable-subtitle: Not even the SPD is willing to go this far.
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 5; unemployed_kpd += 5; kpd_relation += 10; rfb_strength += 50; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; rfb_militancy += 0.1

The demonstration proceeds peacefully, with a minimal police presence. Onlookers admire the strength of the Communist workers, and perhaps some of our members have been peeled off. While we remain suspicous, many are thankful for this act of toloration.


@join
choose-if: spd_relation >= 45 or (united_front_maintained = 1 and spd_relation <=35)
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD has no reason to join.
on-arrival: kpd_relation += 15; workers_kpd += 5; unemployed_kpd += 5; workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 5; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 5; coalition_dissent += 2; communist_coalition += 2; rfb_strength += 100; rfb_militancy += 0.1; sa_strength += 50; sh_strength += 50; marxist_leninist_dissent +=5; left_opposition_dissent +=10
achievement: die_rote_fahne

After some convincing, are leadership accepts the SPD's participation with some grumbling. The display of proletarian unity inspires the workers and terrifies the bourgeoisie and middle class along with the SPD's coalition partners. The far-right paramilitaries increase their recruitment to counter us.
